<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Northam back in loss, Sept qtr output down.</title>
<headline>Northam back in loss, Sept qtr output down.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-Sept versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss before capital spending	  7.39  vs 8.17 profit</p>
<p>    Capital spending				2.18  vs 4.09</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled				400,000  vs 420,000</p>
<p>    Head grade (gram/t)			   6.13  vs   6.10</p>
<p>    Precious metals in concentrates (oz)  75,365  vs 77,421</p>
<p>    Sales					    96.26  vs 106.42</p>
<p>    Cost of sales				 105.82  vs 102.52</p>
<p>Full name: Northam Platinum Ltd, managed by Gold Fields of South Africa Ltd.</p>
<p>NOTE - Mine violence which started on August 9 resulted in the departure of 660 workers and this was the direct cause of lower production, the company said. Replacement workers have been recruited.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
